IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- Part 5 Division 3, ss 178 to 181 -- the right to demand a poll, quorum, chairperson and voting, a member's rights at meetings, proxies.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Imports the core and the keel's s 4(1) definitions ("company limited by shares", "banking corporation").
-- Percentages are tested by integer comparison (a count times 100 against the percentage times the total), never by division, so that an exact 5% counts as "not less than 5%".
-- Sections 64 and 64A (sga1) and s 41(8) and (9) (sgi) are later or other parts: whether they make other provision is an input.

§ `Section 178(1): the right to demand a poll`

-- (a): a constitution provision "is void insofar as it would have the effect of excluding the right to demand a poll at a general meeting on any question or matter other than the election of the
-- chairperson of the meeting or the adjournment of the meeting". Outside "insofar as", and for the two carved-out matters, the section is silent: NOTHING (a scope limit with no "only"; F-24).
-- src:16016 | 178.—(1) Any provision in a company’s constitution is void insofar
-- src:16017 | as it would have the effect —
-- src:16022 | (a) of excluding the right to demand a poll at a general meeting
-- src:16023 | on any question or matter other than the election of the
-- src:16024 | chairperson of the meeting or the adjournment of the
-- src:16025 | meeting;
@ref s 178(1)(a) (src:16016-16025)
GIVEN `the provision has the effect of excluding the right to demand a poll at a general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question or matter is the election of the chairperson of the meeting or the adjournment of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 178(1)(a) the constitution provision is void insofar as it excludes the right to demand a poll` MEANS
    IF `the provision has the effect of excluding the right to demand a poll at a general meeting` AND (NOT `the question or matter is the election of the chairperson of the meeting or the adjournment of the meeting`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is void insofar as it would have the effect of excluding the right to demand a poll ... on any question or matter other than the election of the chairperson of the meeting or the adjournment of the meeting" (F-24)

-- (b): void insofar as it would make ineffective a demand made (i) by not less than 5 members having the right to vote; (ii) by members representing not less than 5% of the total voting rights; or
-- (iii) by members holding shares on which an aggregate sum paid up is not less than 5% of the total sum paid up on all the shares conferring the right to vote.
-- src:16027 | (b) of making ineffective a demand for a poll on any question
-- src:16028 | or matter other than the election of the chairperson of the
-- src:16029 | meeting or the adjournment of the meeting that is made —
-- src:16031 | (i) by not less than 5 members having the right to vote at
-- src:16032 | the meeting;
-- src:16034 | (ii) by a member or members representing not less than
-- src:16035 | 5% of the total voting rights of all the members
-- src:16036 | having the right to vote at the meeting; or
-- src:16038 | (iii) by a member or members holding shares in the
-- src:16039 | company conferring a right to vote at the meeting,
-- src:16040 | being shares on which an aggregate sum has been
-- src:16041 | paid up equal to not less than 5% of the total sum
-- src:16042 | paid up on all the shares conferring that right; or
@ref s 178(1)(b) (src:16027-16042)
GIVEN `the provision has the effect of making a demand for a poll ineffective` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question or matter is the election of the chairperson of the meeting or the adjournment of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of members making the demand who have the right to vote at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `the voting rights represented by the members making the demand` IS A NUMBER
      `the total voting rights of all the members having the right to vote at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `the sum paid up on the shares the members making the demand hold that confer a right to vote at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `the total sum paid up on all the shares conferring that right` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 178(1)(b) the constitution provision is void insofar as it makes the demand ineffective` MEANS
    IF    `the provision has the effect of making a demand for a poll ineffective`
      AND (NOT `the question or matter is the election of the chairperson of the meeting or the adjournment of the meeting`)
      AND (    `the number of members making the demand who have the right to vote at the meeting` AT LEAST 5
            OR (`the total voting rights of all the members having the right to vote at the meeting` GREATER THAN 0 AND 100 TIMES `the voting rights represented by the members making the demand` AT LEAST 5 TIMES `the total voting rights of all the members having the right to vote at the meeting`)
            OR (`the total sum paid up on all the shares conferring that right` GREATER THAN 0 AND 100 TIMES `the sum paid up on the shares the members making the demand hold that confer a right to vote at the meeting` AT LEAST 5 TIMES `the total sum paid up on all the shares conferring that right`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "void insofar as it would have the effect of making ineffective a demand for a poll ... that is made (i) by not less than 5 members ...; (ii) ... not less than 5% ...; or (iii) ... not less than 5%" (F-24)

-- (c): void insofar as it would require the instrument appointing a proxy, or any other document necessary to show the validity of the appointment, to be received "more than 72 hours before a meeting
-- or adjourned meeting in order that the appointment may be effective thereat". A requirement of 72 hours or less is outside the voiding: NOTHING.
-- src:16044 | (c) of requiring the instrument appointing a proxy or any other
-- src:16045 | document necessary to show the validity of or otherwise
-- src:16046 | relating to the appointment of a proxy to be received by the
-- src:16047 | company or any other person more than 72 hours before a
-- src:16048 | meeting or adjourned meeting in order that the
-- src:16049 | appointment may be effective thereat.
@ref s 178(1)(c) (src:16044-16049)
GIVEN `the number of hours before the meeting or adjourned meeting by which the provision requires the instrument or other document to be received` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 178(1)(c) the constitution provision is void insofar as it requires receipt more than 72 hours before the meeting` MEANS
    IF `the number of hours before the meeting or adjourned meeting by which the provision requires the instrument or other document to be received` GREATER THAN 72
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "requiring the instrument appointing a proxy ... to be received by the company or any other person more than 72 hours before a meeting or adjourned meeting" -- a requirement of 72 hours or less is outside the voiding (periods ruling (c); F-24)

-- (1A): "Despite subsection (1)(b), where any provision of the constitution of a company incorporated before 3 January 2016 is void under subsection (1)(b)(ii) or (iii), a demand for a poll on any question
-- or matter other than the election of the chairperson ... or the adjournment ... may be made (a) by a member or members representing not less than 5% of the total voting rights ...; or (b) by a member or members
-- holding shares ... on which an aggregate sum has been paid up equal to not less than 5% of the total sum paid up". A grant gated by "where": JUST FALSE when the gate fails, as the periods ruling's rule (b) gives it
-- (split site (ii); F-25); inside the gate, a demand that falls short of both 5% limbs is outside the grant: NOTHING.
-- src:16053 | (1A) Despite subsection (1)(b), where any provision of the
-- src:16054 | constitution of a company incorporated before 3 January 2016 is
-- src:16055 | void under subsection (1)(b)(ii) or (iii), a demand for a poll on any
-- src:16056 | question or matter other than the election of the chairperson of the
-- src:16057 | meeting or the adjournment of the meeting may be made —
-- src:16059 | (a) by a member or members representing not less than 5% of
-- src:16060 | the total voting rights of all the members having the right to
-- src:16061 | vote at the meeting; or
-- src:16063 | (b) by a member or members holding shares in the company
-- src:16064 | conferring a right to vote at the meeting, being shares on
-- src:16065 | which an aggregate sum has been paid up equal to not less
-- src:16070 | than 5% of the total sum paid up on all the shares
-- src:16071 | conferring that right.
@ref s 178(1A) (src:16053-16071)
GIVEN `the date the company was incorporated` IS A DATE
      `the constitution provision is void under section 178(1)(b)(ii) or (iii)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question or matter is the election of the chairperson of the meeting or the adjournment of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the voting rights represented by the members making the demand` IS A NUMBER
      `the total voting rights of all the members having the right to vote at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `the sum paid up on the shares the members making the demand hold that confer a right to vote at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `the total sum paid up on all the shares conferring that right` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 178(1A) a demand for a poll may be made` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the date the company was incorporated` LESS THAN `the day 3 January 2016` AND `the constitution provision is void under section 178(1)(b)(ii) or (iii)` AND (NOT `the question or matter is the election of the chairperson of the meeting or the adjournment of the meeting`))
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where any provision of the constitution of a company incorporated before 3 January 2016 is void under subsection (1)(b)(ii) or (iii), a demand ... may be made" (a "where" gate on a "may"; periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); split site (ii), F-25)
    ELSE (IF    (`the total voting rights of all the members having the right to vote at the meeting` GREATER THAN 0 AND 100 TIMES `the voting rights represented by the members making the demand` AT LEAST 5 TIMES `the total voting rights of all the members having the right to vote at the meeting`)
             OR (`the total sum paid up on all the shares conferring that right` GREATER THAN 0 AND 100 TIMES `the sum paid up on the shares the members making the demand hold that confer a right to vote at the meeting` AT LEAST 5 TIMES `the total sum paid up on all the shares conferring that right`)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) by a member or members representing not less than 5% of the total voting rights ...; or (b) by a member or members holding shares ... not less than 5% of the total sum paid up" (the demand is outside both limbs of the grant)

-- src:16075 | (2) The instrument appointing a proxy to vote at a meeting of a
-- src:16076 | company is deemed to confer authority to demand or join in
-- src:16077 | demanding a poll, and for the purposes of subsection (1) a demand by
-- src:16078 | a person as proxy for a member of the company is deemed to be the
-- src:16079 | same as a demand by the member.
@ref s 178(2) (src:16075-16079)
GIVEN `the instrument appoints a proxy to vote at a meeting of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 178(2) the instrument appointing a proxy confers authority to demand or join in demanding a poll` MEANS
    IF `the instrument appoints a proxy to vote at a meeting of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of "the instrument appointing a proxy to vote at a meeting of a company"

-- "a demand by a person as proxy for a member of the company is deemed to be the same as a demand by the member": the members whose demand counts are those who demand themselves and those for whom a proxy demands.
@ref s 178(2) (src:16075-16079)
GIVEN `the number of members who demand a poll themselves` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of other members for whom a proxy demands a poll` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 178(2) the number of members whose demand is counted` MEANS
    `the number of members who demand a poll themselves` PLUS `the number of other members for whom a proxy demands a poll`

-- src:16081 | (3) A person entitled to vote on a poll at a meeting is deemed to be a
-- src:16082 | person entitled to vote for the purposes of this Act.
@ref s 178(3) (src:16081-16082)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to vote on a poll at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 178(3) the person is a person entitled to vote for the purposes of this Act` MEANS
    IF `the person is entitled to vote on a poll at the meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection deems a person entitled to vote on a poll to be entitled to vote; it says nothing of a person not so entitled

§ `Section 179: quorum, chairperson, voting and corporate representatives`

-- (1)(a): "So far as the constitution does not make other provision in that behalf and subject to sections 64 and 64A -- (a) 2 members of the company personally present form a quorum". Where the constitution
-- or s 64 or 64A makes other provision, the text points elsewhere: NOTHING. Fewer than 2 members do not form the default quorum: JUST FALSE, read as a definition of the quorum (the other reading, NOTHING under
-- the scope-limit ruling (c), is fork line F-22).
-- src:16086 | 179.—(1) So far as the constitution does not make other provision
-- src:16087 | in that behalf and subject to sections 64 and 64A —
-- src:16089 | (a) 2 members of the company personally present form a
-- src:16090 | quorum;
@ref s 179(1)(a) (src:16086-16090)
GIVEN `the constitution makes other provision on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 64 or 64A makes other provision on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of members of the company personally present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 179(1)(a) the members personally present form a quorum` MEANS
    IF `the constitution makes other provision on the matter` OR `section 64 or 64A makes other provision on the matter`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "So far as the constitution does not make other provision in that behalf and subject to sections 64 and 64A"
    ELSE (IF `the number of members of the company personally present` AT LEAST 2
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "2 members of the company personally present form a quorum" (read as the definition of the default quorum; F-22)

-- The number of members "personally present": those present in person, those attending by virtual meeting technology where s 173J(4)(b) so provides, and corporations deemed personally present by s 179(4).
GIVEN `the number of members physically present at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members attending the meeting using virtual meeting technology` IS A NUMBER
      `section 173J(4)(b) applies to the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of corporate members deemed to be personally present by section 179(4)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 179(1)(a) the number of members of the company personally present, counting those section 173J(4)(b) and section 179(4) add` MEANS
    `the number of members physically present at the meeting` PLUS (IF `section 173J(4)(b) applies to the meeting` THEN `the number of members attending the meeting using virtual meeting technology` ELSE 0) PLUS `the number of corporate members deemed to be personally present by section 179(4)`

-- (1)(b): "any member elected by the members present at a meeting may be chairperson thereof". A grant limited by its own wording: a member not so elected is outside it (NOTHING, F-26).
-- src:16092 | (b) any member elected by the members present at a meeting
-- src:16093 | may be chairperson thereof;
@ref s 179(1)(b) (src:16092-16093)
GIVEN `the constitution makes other provision on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 64 or 64A makes other provision on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member has been elected by the members present at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 179(1)(b) the member may be chairperson of the meeting` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the constitution makes other provision on the matter` OR `section 64 or 64A makes other provision on the matter`)) AND `the member has been elected by the members present at the meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any member elected by the members present at a meeting may be chairperson thereof" (a grant whose condition is unmet, or displaced by the constitution; F-26)

-- (1)(c)(i): "in the case of a company having a share capital -- on a show of hands, each member who is personally present and entitled to vote has one vote".
-- src:16095 | (c) in the case of a company having a share capital —
-- src:16097 | (i) on a show of hands, each member who is personally
-- src:16098 | present and entitled to vote has one vote; and
-- src:16100 | (ii) on a poll, each member has one vote in respect of
-- src:16101 | each share held by the member and where all or part
-- src:16102 | of the share capital consists of stock or units of stock
-- src:16103 | each member has one vote in respect of the stock or
-- src:16104 | units of stock held by the member which is or are or
-- src:16105 | were originally equivalent to one share; and
@ref s 179(1)(c) (src:16095-16105)
GIVEN `the constitution makes other provision on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 64 or 64A makes other provision on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member is personally present` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member is entitled to vote` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 179(1)(c)(i) the number of votes the member has on a show of hands` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the constitution makes other provision on the matter` OR `section 64 or 64A makes other provision on the matter`)) AND `the company has a share capital` AND `the member is personally present` AND `the member is entitled to vote`
    THEN JUST 1
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of a company having a share capital -- on a show of hands, each member who is personally present and entitled to vote has one vote"; otherwise the constitution, section 64 or 64A governs, or the paragraph is silent

-- (1)(c)(ii): "on a poll, each member has one vote in respect of each share held by the member and where all or part of the share capital consists of stock or units of stock each member has one vote in respect of
-- the stock or units of stock held by the member which is or are or were originally equivalent to one share".
@ref s 179(1)(c) (src:16095-16105)
GIVEN `the constitution makes other provision on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 64 or 64A makes other provision on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of shares held by the member` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of units of stock held by the member which are or were originally equivalent to one share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 179(1)(c)(ii) the number of votes the member has on a poll` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the constitution makes other provision on the matter` OR `section 64 or 64A makes other provision on the matter`)) AND `the company has a share capital`
    THEN JUST (`the number of shares held by the member` PLUS `the number of units of stock held by the member which are or were originally equivalent to one share`)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of a company having a share capital -- on a poll, each member has one vote in respect of each share held"; otherwise the constitution, section 64 or 64A governs, or the paragraph is silent

-- src:16107 | (d) in the case of a company not having a share capital every
-- src:16108 | member has one vote.
@ref s 179(1)(d) (src:16107-16108)
GIVEN `the constitution makes other provision on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 64 or 64A makes other provision on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 179(1)(d) the number of votes every member has` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the constitution makes other provision on the matter` OR `section 64 or 64A makes other provision on the matter`)) AND (NOT `the company has a share capital`)
    THEN JUST 1
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of a company not having a share capital every member has one vote"; otherwise the constitution, section 64 or 64A governs, or the paragraph is silent

-- src:16112 | (2) On a poll taken at a meeting a person entitled to more than
-- src:16113 | one vote need not, if the person votes, use all the person’s votes or
-- src:16114 | cast all the votes the person uses in the same way.
@ref s 179(2) (src:16112-16114)
GIVEN `the vote is on a poll` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of votes the person is entitled to` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 179(2) the person need not use all the person's votes or cast all the votes the person uses in the same way` MEANS
    IF NOT `the vote is on a poll`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On a poll taken at a meeting a person ... need not" (an "on"/"when" gate on a liberty, counted as "where" by the periods ruling item (b) and the 2026-11-05 delegated-definitions ruling item (c); split site (ii), F-32)
    ELSE (IF `the number of votes the person is entitled to` GREATER THAN 1
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person entitled to more than one vote need not" -- a person with one vote is outside the subsection

-- (3): a corporation "may by resolution of its directors or other governing body -- (a) if it is a member of a company -- authorise such person as it thinks fit to act as its representative ...; or (b) if it is a creditor,
-- including a holder of debentures, of a company -- authorise such person ... at all meetings of any creditors". A power with "if" gates: NOTHING when a gate fails (F-27).
-- src:16119 | (3) A corporation may by resolution of its directors or other
-- src:16120 | governing body —
-- src:16122 | (a) if it is a member of a company — authorise such person as
-- src:16123 | it thinks fit to act as its representative either at a particular
-- src:16124 | meeting or at all meetings of the company or of any class of
-- src:16125 | members; or
-- src:16127 | (b) if it is a creditor, including a holder of debentures, of a
-- src:16128 | company — authorise such person as it thinks fit to act as
-- src:16129 | its representative either at a particular meeting or at all
-- src:16130 | meetings of any creditors of the company,
-- src:16132 | and a person so authorised is, in accordance with the person’s
-- src:16133 | authority and until the person’s authority is revoked by the
-- src:16134 | corporation, entitled to exercise the same powers on behalf of the
-- src:16135 | corporation as the corporation could exercise if it were an individual
-- src:16136 | member, creditor or holder of debentures of the company.
@ref s 179(3) (src:16119-16136)
GIVEN `the corporation is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is a creditor, including a holder of debentures, of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has authorised the person by resolution of its directors or other governing body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 179(3) the corporation may authorise the person to act as its representative` MEANS
    IF `the corporation has authorised the person by resolution of its directors or other governing body` AND (`the corporation is a member of the company` OR `the corporation is a creditor, including a holder of debentures, of the company`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A corporation may by resolution of its directors or other governing body -- (a) if it is a member of a company -- authorise ...; or (b) if it is a creditor ... -- authorise" (F-27)

-- "a person so authorised is, in accordance with the person's authority and until the person's authority is revoked by the corporation, entitled to exercise the same powers on behalf of the corporation as the
-- corporation could exercise if it were an individual member, creditor or holder of debentures". "Until": after revocation, JUST FALSE (periods ruling (a)); acting outside the authority is outside the entitlement (NOTHING).
@ref s 179(3) (src:16119-16136)
GIVEN `the person has been authorised under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts in accordance with the person's authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has revoked the person's authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 179(3) the person so authorised is entitled to exercise the corporation's powers` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person has been authorised under subsection (3)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the entitlement is that of "a person so authorised"
    ELSE (IF `the corporation has revoked the person's authority`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the person's authority is revoked by the corporation" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling (a))
          ELSE (IF `the person acts in accordance with the person's authority` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in accordance with the person's authority" (an entitled-named function: the general rule, listed in F-28)

-- src:16138 | (4) Where —
-- src:16140 | (a) a person present at a meeting is authorised to act as the
-- src:16141 | representative of a corporation at the meeting by virtue of
-- src:16142 | an authority given by the corporation under subsection (3);
-- src:16143 | and
-- src:16145 | (b) the person is not otherwise entitled to be present at the
-- src:16146 | meeting as a member or proxy or as a corporate
-- src:16147 | representative of another member,
-- src:16149 | the corporation is, for the purposes of subsection (1), deemed to be
-- src:16150 | personally present at the meeting.
@ref s 179(4) (src:16138-16150)
GIVEN `the person present at the meeting is authorised to act as the representative of the corporation at the meeting by virtue of an authority given under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is not otherwise entitled to be present at the meeting as a member or proxy or as a corporate representative of another member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 179(4) the corporation is deemed to be personally present at the meeting` MEANS
    IF `the person present at the meeting is authorised to act as the representative of the corporation at the meeting by virtue of an authority given under subsection (3)` AND `the person is not otherwise entitled to be present at the meeting as a member or proxy or as a corporate representative of another member`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where -- (a) a person present at a meeting is authorised to act as the representative of a corporation ...; and (b) the person is not otherwise entitled to be present ... the corporation is ... deemed to be personally present" (a "where" gate on a deeming)

-- src:16154 | (5) Subject to section 41(8) and (9), a certificate under the seal of
-- src:16155 | the corporation is prima facie evidence of the appointment or of the
-- src:16156 | revocation of the appointment (as the case may be) of a representative
-- src:16157 | pursuant to subsection (3).
@ref s 179(5) (src:16154-16157)
GIVEN `section 41(8) or (9) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate is under the seal of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate is of the appointment or of the revocation of the appointment of a representative under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 179(5) the certificate is prima facie evidence of the appointment or of the revocation of the appointment` MEANS
    IF `section 41(8) or (9) applies`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to section 41(8) and (9)" -- those subsections (a later part's) govern where they apply
    ELSE (IF `the certificate is under the seal of the corporation` AND `the certificate is of the appointment or of the revocation of the appointment of a representative under subsection (3)`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of "a certificate under the seal of the corporation" of the appointment or its revocation

-- src:16159 | (6) Where a holding company is beneficially entitled to the whole
-- src:16160 | of the issued shares of a subsidiary and a minute is signed by a
-- src:16161 | representative of the holding company authorised pursuant to
-- src:16162 | subsection (3) stating that any act, matter, or thing, or any ordinary
-- src:16163 | or special resolution, required by this Act or by the constitution of the
-- src:16168 | subsidiary to be made, performed, or passed by or at an ordinary
-- src:16169 | general meeting or an extraordinary general meeting of the subsidiary
-- src:16170 | has been made, performed, or passed, that act, matter, thing, or
-- src:16171 | resolution is, for all purposes, deemed to have been duly made,
-- src:16172 | performed, or passed by or at an ordinary general meeting, or as the
-- src:16173 | case requires, by or at an extraordinary general meeting of the
-- src:16174 | subsidiary.
@ref s 179(6) (src:16159-16174)
GIVEN `a holding company is beneficially entitled to the whole of the issued shares of the subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a minute is signed by a representative of the holding company authorised pursuant to subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the minute states that the act, matter, thing, or ordinary or special resolution required by this Act or by the constitution of the subsidiary to be made, performed or passed by or at a general meeting has been made, performed or passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 179(6) the act, matter, thing or resolution is deemed to have been duly made, performed or passed` MEANS
    IF `a holding company is beneficially entitled to the whole of the issued shares of the subsidiary` AND `a minute is signed by a representative of the holding company authorised pursuant to subsection (3)` AND `the minute states that the act, matter, thing, or ordinary or special resolution required by this Act or by the constitution of the subsidiary to be made, performed or passed by or at a general meeting has been made, performed or passed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a holding company is beneficially entitled to the whole of the issued shares of a subsidiary and a minute is signed by a representative ... stating that ... has been made, performed, or passed, that act ... is, for all purposes, deemed to have been duly made" (a "where" gate on a deeming)

-- (7): "Where by or under any provision of this Act any notice, copy of a resolution or other document relating to any matter is required to be lodged by a company with the Registrar, and a minute mentioned
-- in subsection (6) is signed by the representative ... and the minute relates to such a matter the company must within 14 days after the signing of the minute lodge a copy thereof with the Registrar."
-- src:16178 | (7) Where by or under any provision of this Act any notice, copy of
-- src:16179 | a resolution or other document relating to any matter is required to be
-- src:16180 | lodged by a company with the Registrar, and a minute mentioned in
-- src:16181 | subsection (6) is signed by the representative pursuant to that
-- src:16182 | subsection and the minute relates to such a matter the company must
-- src:16183 | within 14 days after the signing of the minute lodge a copy thereof
-- src:16184 | with the Registrar.
@ref s 179(7) (src:16178-16184)
GIVEN `a notice, copy of a resolution or other document relating to the matter is required to be lodged by the company with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a minute mentioned in subsection (6) is signed by the representative and relates to that matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the minute was signed` IS A DATE
      `the date the company lodged a copy of the minute with the Registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 179(7) the company has lodged a copy of the minute with the Registrar in time` MEANS
    IF NOT (`a notice, copy of a resolution or other document relating to the matter is required to be lodged by the company with the Registrar` AND `a minute mentioned in subsection (6) is signed by the representative and relates to that matter`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where ... a notice, copy of a resolution or other document ... is required to be lodged ... and a minute mentioned in subsection (6) is signed ... the company must" (a "where" gate on a duty)
    ELSE (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date the minute was signed` `the date the company lodged a copy of the minute with the Registrar` 14 Days
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must within 14 days after the signing of the minute lodge a copy thereof with the Registrar" (a duty's own question; a period the text fixes)

GIVEN `the date the minute was signed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 179(7) the number of days from the signing to the last day for lodging` MEANS
    (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date the minute was signed` 14 Days) MINUS `the date the minute was signed`

-- src:16188 | (8) For the purposes of this section, any reference to a member of a
-- src:16189 | company does not include the company itself where it is such a
-- src:16190 | member by virtue of its holding shares as treasury shares.
@ref s 179(8) (src:16188-16190)
GIVEN `the company holds shares in itself as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 179(8) the company is a member for the purposes of this section` MEANS
    IF `the company holds shares in itself as treasury shares`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any reference to a member of a company does not include the company itself where it is such a member by virtue of its holding shares as treasury shares" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of the company as a member by virtue of treasury shares

§ `Section 180: a member's rights at meetings`

-- "A member has, despite any provision in the constitution of the company, a right to attend any general meeting of the company and to speak on any resolution before the meeting." An entitlement ("has a right"),
-- listed among the entitled-named functions (F-28). A person who is not a member is outside the subsection: NOTHING.
-- src:16194 | 180.—(1) A member has, despite any provision in the constitution
-- src:16195 | of the company, a right to attend any general meeting of the company
-- src:16196 | and to speak on any resolution before the meeting.
@ref s 180(1) (src:16194-16196)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 180(1) the member has the right to attend any general meeting and to speak on any resolution before the meeting` MEANS
    IF `the person is a member of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection gives the right to "a member" and says nothing of anyone else

-- src:16200 | (2) In the case of a company limited by shares, the holder of a share
-- src:16201 | may vote on a resolution before a general meeting of the company if,
-- src:16202 | in accordance with the provisions of section 64, the share confers on
-- src:16203 | the holder a right to vote on that resolution.
@ref s 180(2) (src:16200-16203)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
      `the share confers on the holder a right to vote on that resolution in accordance with section 64` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 180(2) the holder of the share may vote on the resolution` MEANS
    IF `s 4(1) "company limited by shares" the company is a company limited by shares` liability EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the share confers on the holder a right to vote on that resolution in accordance with section 64`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a company limited by shares, the holder of a share may vote on a resolution ... if, in accordance with the provisions of section 64, the share confers on the holder a right to vote" (a grant whose "if" gate failed, or a company outside the subsection; F-29)

-- src:16207 | (3) In the case of a company other than a company limited by
-- src:16208 | shares, a member may vote on a resolution before a general meeting
-- src:16209 | of the company if the right to vote on that resolution is conferred on
-- src:16210 | the member under the constitution of the company.
@ref s 180(3) (src:16207-16210)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
      `the right to vote on that resolution is conferred on the member under the constitution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 180(3) the member may vote on the resolution` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`s 4(1) "company limited by shares" the company is a company limited by shares` liability EQUALS JUST TRUE)) AND `the right to vote on that resolution is conferred on the member under the constitution of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of a company other than a company limited by shares, a member may vote on a resolution ... if the right to vote on that resolution is conferred on the member under the constitution" (a grant whose "if" gate failed, or a company outside the subsection; F-29)

`s 180(4) the day 15 August 1984` MEANS Date 15 8 1984

-- (4): "Despite subsection (2), a preference share issued after 15 August 1984 but before 3 January 2016 carries, in addition to any other right ..., the right in a poll at any general meeting to at least one vote in
-- respect of each such share held during such period as the preferential dividend or any part thereof remains in arrears and unpaid, such period starting from a date not more than 12 months, or such lesser period as
-- the constitution may provide, after the due date of the dividend." The period starts on the date the constitution fixes, but not later than the last day of the 12 months (or lesser period) after the due date.
-- src:16214 | (4) Despite subsection (2), a preference share issued after
-- src:16215 | 15 August 1984 but before 3 January 2016 carries, in addition to
-- src:16220 | any other right conferred by this Act, the right in a poll at any general
-- src:16221 | meeting to at least one vote in respect of each such share held during
-- src:16222 | such period as the preferential dividend or any part thereof remains in
-- src:16223 | arrears and unpaid, such period starting from a date not more than
-- src:16224 | 12 months, or such lesser period as the constitution may provide, after
-- src:16225 | the due date of the dividend.
@ref s 180(4) (src:16214-16225)
GIVEN `the date the share was issued` IS A DATE
      `the share is a preference share within subsection (5)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dividend or any part of it remains in arrears and unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the due date of the dividend` IS A DATE
      `the lesser period in months the constitution provides` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the date from which the constitution starts the period` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 180(4) the preference share carries the right to at least one vote on a poll in respect of the share` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the date the share was issued` GREATER THAN `s 180(4) the day 15 August 1984` AND `the date the share was issued` LESS THAN `the day 3 January 2016` AND `the share is a preference share within subsection (5)(a)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a preference share issued after 15 August 1984 but before 3 January 2016" (a scope limit with no "only"; periods ruling (c))
    ELSE (IF NOT `the dividend or any part of it remains in arrears and unpaid`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "during such period as the preferential dividend or any part thereof remains in arrears and unpaid"
          ELSE (CONSIDER `the date from which the constitution starts the period`
                WHEN JUST started THEN
                    (IF `the date asked` AT LEAST (IF started LESS THAN `s 180(4) the latest day on which the period may start` `the due date of the dividend` `the lesser period in months the constitution provides` THEN started ELSE `s 180(4) the latest day on which the period may start` `the due date of the dividend` `the lesser period in months the constitution provides`)
                     THEN JUST TRUE
                     ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "such period starting from a date not more than 12 months, or such lesser period as the constitution may provide, after the due date of the dividend" (before the day the constitution starts the period, which the text caps; a period the text fixes, periods ruling (a); F-33)
                WHEN NOTHING THEN
                    (IF `the date asked` AT LEAST `s 180(4) the latest day on which the period may start` `the due date of the dividend` `the lesser period in months the constitution provides`
                     THEN JUST TRUE
                     ELSE NOTHING)))   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text fixes only the latest day on which the period may start ("not more than 12 months ... after the due date"); where the constitution fixes no day, an earlier day is for the constitution and is asked as an input (F-33)

GIVEN `the due date of the dividend` IS A DATE
      `the lesser period in months the constitution provides` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 180(4) the latest day on which the period may start` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the lesser period in months the constitution provides`
    WHEN JUST lesser THEN `period: the last day of a period after` `the due date of the dividend` lesser Months
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `period: the last day of a period after` `the due date of the dividend` 12 Months

-- src:16229 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (4) —
-- src:16231 | (a) “preference share” means a share, by whatever name
-- src:16232 | called, which does not entitle the holder thereof —
-- src:16234 | (i) to the right to vote at a general meeting (except in the
-- src:16235 | circumstances specified in subsection (4)); or
-- src:16237 | (ii) to any right to participate beyond a specified amount
-- src:16238 | in any distribution whether by way of dividend, or on
-- src:16239 | redemption, in a winding up, or otherwise; and
@ref s 180(5)(a) (src:16229-16239)
GIVEN `the share does not entitle the holder to the right to vote at a general meeting, except in the circumstances specified in subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the share does not entitle the holder to any right to participate beyond a specified amount in any distribution, whether by way of dividend, or on redemption, in a winding up, or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 180(5)(a) the share is a preference share` MEANS
    IF `the share does not entitle the holder to the right to vote at a general meeting, except in the circumstances specified in subsection (4)` AND `the share does not entitle the holder to any right to participate beyond a specified amount in any distribution, whether by way of dividend, or on redemption, in a winding up, or otherwise`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'preference share' means a share, by whatever name called, which does not entitle the holder thereof (i) to the right to vote ...; or (ii) to any right to participate beyond a specified amount in any distribution" (a "means" definition; "does not entitle ... (i) ...; or (ii) ..." is read as neither, F-23)

-- src:16241 | (b) a dividend is deemed to be due on the date appointed in the
-- src:16242 | constitution for the payment of the dividend for any year or
-- src:16243 | other period or, if no such date is appointed, upon the day
-- src:16244 | immediately following the expiration of the year or other
-- src:16245 | period and whether or not such dividend has been earned or
-- src:16246 | declared.
@ref s 180(5)(b) (src:16241-16246)
GIVEN `the date appointed in the constitution for the payment of the dividend for the year or other period` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the last day of the year or other period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 180(5)(b) the date on which the dividend is deemed to be due` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date appointed in the constitution for the payment of the dividend for the year or other period`
    WHEN JUST appointed THEN appointed
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `period: the last day of a period after` `the last day of the year or other period` 1 Days

§ `Section 181: proxies`

-- src:16252 | 181.—(1) Subject to this section, a member of a company entitled
-- src:16253 | to attend and vote at a meeting of the company, or at a meeting of any
-- src:16254 | class of members of the company, is entitled to appoint another
-- src:16255 | person, whether a member or not, as the member’s proxy to attend
-- src:16256 | and vote instead of the member at the meeting and a proxy appointed
-- src:16257 | to attend and vote instead of a member also has the same right as the
-- src:16258 | member to speak at the meeting.
@ref s 181(1) (src:16252-16258)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member is entitled to attend and vote at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 181(1) the member is entitled to appoint another person as the member's proxy` MEANS
    IF `the person is a member of the company` AND `the member is entitled to attend and vote at the meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a member of a company entitled to attend and vote at a meeting ... is entitled to appoint another person ... as the member's proxy" (an entitlement whose condition is unmet; listed among the entitled-named functions, F-28)

@ref s 181(1) (src:16252-16258)
GIVEN `the person has been appointed as proxy to attend and vote instead of a member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 181(1) the proxy has the same right as the member to speak at the meeting` MEANS
    IF `the person has been appointed as proxy to attend and vote instead of a member`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "a proxy appointed to attend and vote instead of a member also has the same right as the member to speak" speaks only of such a proxy

-- (1A)(a): "unless the constitution otherwise provides -- a proxy is not entitled to vote except on a poll": a bar. JUST TRUE means the proxy is barred from voting on a question not decided on a poll.
-- src:16262 | (1A) Subject to this section, unless the constitution otherwise
-- src:16263 | provides —
-- src:16265 | (a) a proxy is not entitled to vote except on a poll;
-- src:16270 | (b) a member is not entitled to appoint more than 2 proxies to
-- src:16271 | attend and vote at the same meeting; and
-- src:16273 | (c) where a member appoints 2 proxies, the appointments are
-- src:16274 | invalid unless the member specifies the proportions of the
-- src:16275 | member’s holdings to be represented by each proxy.
@ref s 181(1A) (src:16262-16275)
GIVEN `the constitution otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proxy was appointed under subsection (1C)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the question is decided on a poll` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 181(1A)(a) the proxy is barred from voting on the question` MEANS
    IF `the constitution otherwise provides` OR `the proxy was appointed under subsection (1C)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to this section, unless the constitution otherwise provides" -- the constitution, or subsection (1D) for a proxy appointed under (1C), governs
    ELSE (IF `the question is decided on a poll`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a proxy is not entitled to vote except on a poll" -- this is a poll, so this paragraph does not bar the vote
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- (1A)(b): "a member is not entitled to appoint more than 2 proxies to attend and vote at the same meeting": a ceiling of two. Subject to (1C) and "unless the constitution otherwise provides".
@ref s 181(1A)(b) (src:16270-16271)
GIVEN `the constitution otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 181(1C) applies to the member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of proxies the member proposes to appoint to attend and vote at the same meeting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 181(1A)(b) the member is entitled to appoint that number of proxies` MEANS
    IF `the constitution otherwise provides` OR `section 181(1C) applies to the member` OR `the number of proxies the member proposes to appoint to attend and vote at the same meeting` LESS THAN 1
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to this section, unless the constitution otherwise provides"; the paragraph says nothing of an appointment of no proxy
    ELSE (IF `the number of proxies the member proposes to appoint to attend and vote at the same meeting` GREATER THAN 2
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a member is not entitled to appoint more than 2 proxies to attend and vote at the same meeting" (a flat negative)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

@ref s 181(1A)(c) (src:16273-16275)
GIVEN `the constitution otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member appoints 2 proxies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member specifies the proportions of the member's holdings to be represented by each proxy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 181(1A)(c) the appointments of the 2 proxies are valid` MEANS
    IF `the constitution otherwise provides` OR (NOT `the member appoints 2 proxies`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the constitution otherwise provides -- where a member appoints 2 proxies" (the paragraph speaks only of two proxies, and gives way to the constitution)
    ELSE (IF `the member specifies the proportions of the member's holdings to be represented by each proxy`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the appointments are invalid unless the member specifies the proportions of the member's holdings to be represented by each proxy"

-- src:16279 | (1B) Despite anything to the contrary in the constitution of a
-- src:16280 | company, a member may appoint a proxy under this section by
-- src:16281 | depositing with the company an instrument of appointment by
-- src:16282 | electronic means.
@ref s 181(1B) (src:16279-16282)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument of appointment is deposited by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 181(1B) the member may appoint a proxy by depositing an instrument of appointment by electronic means` MEANS
    IF `the person is a member of the company` AND `the instrument of appointment is deposited by electronic means`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Despite anything to the contrary in the constitution of a company, a member may appoint a proxy under this section by depositing with the company an instrument of appointment by electronic means" (a grant outside its own wording; F-30)

-- src:16286 | (1BA) The electronic means by which an instrument of
-- src:16287 | appointment may be deposited under subsection (1B) must be
-- src:16288 | specified by the company in the notice of meeting.
@ref s 181(1BA) (src:16286-16288)
GIVEN `the company has specified the electronic means in the notice of meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 181(1BA) the company has specified the electronic means in the notice of meeting` MEANS
    IF `the company has specified the electronic means in the notice of meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The electronic means by which an instrument of appointment may be deposited under subsection (1B) must be specified by the company in the notice of meeting" (a duty's own question)

-- src:16292 | (1C) A member of a company having a share capital who is a
-- src:16293 | relevant intermediary may appoint more than 2 proxies in relation to a
-- src:16294 | meeting to exercise all or any of the member’s rights to attend and to
-- src:16295 | speak and vote at the meeting, but each proxy must be appointed to
-- src:16296 | exercise the rights attached to a different share or shares held by the
-- src:16297 | member (which number and class of shares must be specified).
@ref s 181(1C) (src:16292-16297)
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member is a relevant intermediary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `each proxy is appointed to exercise the rights attached to a different share or shares held by the member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number and class of those shares are specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 181(1C) the member may appoint more than 2 proxies` MEANS
    IF `the company has a share capital` AND `the member is a relevant intermediary` AND `each proxy is appointed to exercise the rights attached to a different share or shares held by the member` AND `the number and class of those shares are specified`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A member of a company having a share capital who is a relevant intermediary may appoint more than 2 proxies ..., but each proxy must be appointed to exercise the rights attached to a different share or shares held by the member (which number and class of shares must be specified)" (F-30)

-- src:16303 | (1D) A proxy appointed under subsection (1C) has at a meeting the
-- src:16304 | right to vote on a show of hands.
@ref s 181(1D) (src:16303-16304)
GIVEN `the proxy was appointed under subsection (1C)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 181(1D) the proxy has the right to vote on a show of hands` MEANS
    IF `the proxy was appointed under subsection (1C)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of a proxy appointed under subsection (1C)

-- src:16308 | (2) In every notice calling a meeting of a company or a meeting of
-- src:16309 | any class of members of a company there must appear with
-- src:16310 | reasonable prominence a statement as to the rights of the member
-- src:16311 | to appoint a proxy or proxies to attend and vote instead of the
-- src:16312 | member, and that a proxy need not also be a member; and if default is
-- src:16313 | made in complying with this subsection as respects any meeting,
-- src:16314 | every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an
-- src:16315 | offence.
@ref s 181(2) (src:16308-16315)
GIVEN `a statement as to the rights of the member to appoint a proxy or proxies to attend and vote instead of the member appears in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement appears with reasonable prominence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states that a proxy need not also be a member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 181(2) the notice contains the statement the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `a statement as to the rights of the member to appoint a proxy or proxies to attend and vote instead of the member appears in the notice` AND `the statement appears with reasonable prominence` AND `the notice states that a proxy need not also be a member`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In every notice calling a meeting ... there must appear with reasonable prominence a statement as to the rights of the member to appoint a proxy or proxies ..., and that a proxy need not also be a member" (a duty's own question)

-- (2) the offence: "if default is made in complying with this subsection as respects any meeting, every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence". No penalty is stated in the subsection.
@ref s 181(2) (src:16308-16315)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (2) as respects the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 181(2) the officer is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with subsection (2) as respects the meeting` AND `the person is an officer of the company who is in default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), F-10): "if default is made in complying with this subsection as respects any meeting, every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet

@ref s 181(2) (src:16308-16315)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (2) as respects the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 181(2) the most the officer may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection makes the officer guilty of an offence and states no fine or term; a penalty provision outside the sources would have to be asked as an input

-- (3) and (4): "Any person who authorises or permits an invitation to appoint as proxy a person or one of a number of persons specified in the invitation to be issued at the company's expense to some only
-- of the members entitled to be sent a notice of the meeting and to vote thereat by proxy shall be guilty of an offence ... fine not exceeding $2,000." "(4) No person shall be guilty of an offence under
-- subsection (3) by reason only of the issue to a member at the member's request of a form of appointment naming the proxy or a list of persons willing to act as proxies if the form or list is available on request
-- in writing to every member entitled to vote at the meeting by proxy." Subsection (4) is read as a defence: when its facts are not shown, "this subsection gives no defence on these facts" (JUST FALSE; F-31).
-- src:16330 | (4) No person shall be guilty of an offence under subsection (3) by
-- src:16331 | reason only of the issue to a member at the member’s request of a
-- src:16332 | form of appointment naming the proxy or a list of persons willing to
-- src:16333 | act as proxies if the form or list is available on request in writing to
-- src:16334 | every member entitled to vote at the meeting by proxy.
@ref s 181(4) (src:16330-16334)
GIVEN `the invitation is the issue to a member at the member's request of a form of appointment naming the proxy or a list of persons willing to act as proxies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form or list is available on request in writing to every member entitled to vote at the meeting by proxy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 181(4) this subsection gives the person a defence to guilt under subsection (3)` MEANS
    IF `the invitation is the issue to a member at the member's request of a form of appointment naming the proxy or a list of persons willing to act as proxies` AND `the form or list is available on request in writing to every member entitled to vote at the meeting by proxy`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall be guilty of an offence under subsection (3) by reason only of the issue to a member at the member's request of a form of appointment ... if the form or list is available on request in writing to every member" (this subsection gives no defence on these facts; delegated defences ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); F-31)

-- src:16319 | (3) Any person who authorises or permits an invitation to appoint as
-- src:16320 | proxy a person or one of a number of persons specified in the
-- src:16325 | invitation to be issued at the company’s expense to some only of the
-- src:16326 | members entitled to be sent a notice of the meeting and to vote thereat
-- src:16327 | by proxy shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction
-- src:16328 | to a fine not exceeding $2,000.
@ref s 181(3) (src:16319-16328)
GIVEN `the person authorises or permits an invitation to appoint as proxy a person or one of a number of persons specified in the invitation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the invitation is issued at the company's expense` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the invitation is issued to some only of the members entitled to be sent a notice of the meeting and to vote at it by proxy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (4) gives the person a defence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 181(3) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `the person authorises or permits an invitation to appoint as proxy a person or one of a number of persons specified in the invitation` AND `the invitation is issued at the company's expense` AND `the invitation is issued to some only of the members entitled to be sent a notice of the meeting and to vote at it by proxy` AND (NOT `subsection (4) gives the person a defence`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), F-10): "Any person who authorises or permits an invitation to appoint as proxy ... to be issued at the company's expense to some only of the members ... shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet, or subsection (4) gives a defence (the "unless" once met, F-31)

@ref s 181(3) (src:16319-16328)
GIVEN `the person authorises or permits an invitation to appoint as proxy a person or one of a number of persons specified in the invitation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the invitation is issued at the company's expense` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the invitation is issued to some only of the members entitled to be sent a notice of the meeting and to vote at it by proxy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (4) gives the person a defence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 181(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 181(3) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the person authorises or permits an invitation to appoint as proxy a person or one of a number of persons specified in the invitation` `the invitation is issued at the company's expense` `the invitation is issued to some only of the members entitled to be sent a notice of the meeting and to vote at it by proxy` `subsection (4) gives the person a defence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 2000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)   -- a fine not exceeding $2,000; no imprisonment; no default penalty stated
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

-- src:16336 | (5) Any person who authorises or permits an invitation to appoint as
-- src:16337 | proxy a person or one of a number of persons specified in the
-- src:16338 | invitation to be issued or circulated shall be guilty of an offence
-- src:16339 | unless the invitation is accompanied by a form of proxy which entitles
-- src:16340 | the member to direct the proxy to vote either for or against the
-- src:16341 | resolution.
@ref s 181(5) (src:16336-16341)
GIVEN `the person authorises or permits an invitation to appoint as proxy a person or one of a number of persons specified in the invitation to be issued or circulated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the invitation is accompanied by a form of proxy which entitles the member to direct the proxy to vote either for or against the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 181(5) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `the person authorises or permits an invitation to appoint as proxy a person or one of a number of persons specified in the invitation to be issued or circulated` AND (NOT `the invitation is accompanied by a form of proxy which entitles the member to direct the proxy to vote either for or against the resolution`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), F-10): "Any person who authorises or permits an invitation ... to be issued or circulated shall be guilty of an offence unless the invitation is accompanied by a form of proxy which entitles the member to direct the proxy to vote either for or against the resolution" -- an element is unmet, or the "unless" is met (F-31)

@ref s 181(5) (src:16336-16341)
GIVEN `the person authorises or permits an invitation to appoint as proxy a person or one of a number of persons specified in the invitation to be issued or circulated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the invitation is accompanied by a form of proxy which entitles the member to direct the proxy to vote either for or against the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 181(5) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection makes the person guilty of an offence and states no fine or term

-- (6) "relevant intermediary" means (a) a banking corporation licensed under the Banking Act 1970 or a wholly-owned subsidiary of such a banking corporation, whose business includes the provision of nominee
-- services and who holds shares in that capacity; (b) a person holding a capital markets services licence to provide custodial services under the Securities and Futures Act 2001 and who holds shares in that
-- capacity; or (c) the Central Provident Fund Board ... in respect of shares purchased under the subsidiary legislation ..., if the Board holds those shares in the capacity of an intermediary.
-- src:16343 | (6) In this section, “relevant intermediary” means —
-- src:16345 | (a) a banking corporation licensed under the Banking
-- src:16346 | Act 1970 or a wholly‑owned subsidiary of such a
-- src:16347 | banking corporation, whose business includes the
-- src:16348 | provision of nominee services and who holds shares in
-- src:16349 | that capacity;
@ref s 181(6)(a) (src:16343-16349)
GIVEN `the member is a bank or merchant bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member is a wholly owned subsidiary of such a banking corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member's business includes the provision of nominee services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member holds shares in the capacity of a provider of nominee services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 181(6)(a) the member is a relevant intermediary because of its banking business` MEANS
    IF    ((`s 4(1) "banking corporation" the body is a banking corporation` `the member is a bank or merchant bank licensed under the Banking Act 1970` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `the member is a wholly owned subsidiary of such a banking corporation`)
      AND `the member's business includes the provision of nominee services` AND `the member holds shares in the capacity of a provider of nominee services`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): ""relevant intermediary" means (a) a banking corporation licensed under the Banking Act 1970 or a wholly-owned subsidiary of such a banking corporation, whose business includes the provision of nominee services and who holds shares in that capacity" (a "means" definition)

-- src:16351 | (b) a person holding a capital markets services licence to
-- src:16352 | provide custodial services under the Securities and Futures
-- src:16353 | Act 2001 and who holds shares in that capacity; or
@ref s 181(6)(b) (src:16351-16353)
GIVEN `the member holds a capital markets services licence to provide custodial services under the Securities and Futures Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member holds shares in the capacity of a provider of custodial services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 181(6)(b) the member is a relevant intermediary because of its custodial licence` MEANS
    IF `the member holds a capital markets services licence to provide custodial services under the Securities and Futures Act 2001` AND `the member holds shares in the capacity of a provider of custodial services`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) a person holding a capital markets services licence to provide custodial services under the Securities and Futures Act 2001 and who holds shares in that capacity" (a "means" definition)

-- src:16355 | (c) the Central Provident Fund Board established by the
-- src:16356 | Central Provident Fund Act 1953, in respect of shares
-- src:16357 | purchased under the subsidiary legislation made under that
-- src:16358 | Act providing for the making of investments from the
-- src:16359 | contributions and interest standing to the credit of
-- src:16360 | members of the Central Provident Fund, if the Board
-- src:16361 | holds those shares in the capacity of an intermediary
-- src:16362 | pursuant to or in accordance with that subsidiary
-- src:16363 | legislation.
@ref s 181(6)(c) (src:16355-16363)
GIVEN `the member is the Central Provident Fund Board established by the Central Provident Fund Act 1953` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares were purchased under the subsidiary legislation made under that Act providing for the making of investments from the contributions and interest standing to the credit of members of the Central Provident Fund` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Board holds those shares in the capacity of an intermediary pursuant to or in accordance with that subsidiary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 181(6)(c) the member is a relevant intermediary because it is the Central Provident Fund Board` MEANS
    IF `the member is the Central Provident Fund Board established by the Central Provident Fund Act 1953` AND `the shares were purchased under the subsidiary legislation made under that Act providing for the making of investments from the contributions and interest standing to the credit of members of the Central Provident Fund` AND `the Board holds those shares in the capacity of an intermediary pursuant to or in accordance with that subsidiary legislation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) the Central Provident Fund Board ..., in respect of shares purchased under the subsidiary legislation ..., if the Board holds those shares in the capacity of an intermediary" (a "means" definition)

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      c IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 181(6) the member is a relevant intermediary` MEANS
    IF a EQUALS JUST TRUE OR b EQUALS JUST TRUE OR c EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): ""relevant intermediary" means (a) ...; (b) ...; or (c) ..." (a "means" definition; none of the three limbs holds)

§ `Regulative rule: the duty of s 179(7)`

DECLARE `s 179 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 179(7) lodge a copy of the minute with the Registrar`

-- The clock: time 0 is the day the minute is signed; the last day is 14 days later.
-- src:16178 | (7) Where by or under any provision of this Act any notice, copy of
-- src:16179 | a resolution or other document relating to any matter is required to be
-- src:16180 | lodged by a company with the Registrar, and a minute mentioned in
-- src:16181 | subsection (6) is signed by the representative pursuant to that
-- src:16182 | subsection and the minute relates to such a matter the company must
-- src:16183 | within 14 days after the signing of the minute lodge a copy thereof
-- src:16184 | with the Registrar.
@ref s 179(7) (src:16178-16184)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 179 act`
`s 179(7) the company must lodge a copy of the minute with the Registrar` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 179(7) lodge a copy of the minute with the Registrar`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not lodge a copy of the minute with the Registrar within 14 days after the signing of the minute"
